## 🛡 ENFORCEMENT MECHANISMS

These principles are enforced through three layers:

### Layer A — Database (most important)
- RLS policies on all chat tables
- NO `OR is_super_admin()` in operational chat policies
- Separate schemas for operational vs infrastructure tables
- Foreign key constraints prevent accidental cross-references

### Layer B — Service / API
- All chat RPCs validate `auth.uid()` membership before returning data
- No RPC accepts both `p_org_id` AND `p_admin_override` parameters in the same signature
- Service files are domain-segregated: `workspace-chat.service.ts`, `chat-tx.service.ts`, `support.service.ts` (future) — they do NOT cross-import

### Layer C — UI / UX
- The Super Admin UI (`SuperAdmin.tsx`) MUST NOT contain any component that imports `workspace-chat.service.ts` or `chat-tx.service.ts`
- The user-facing "Report a problem" button is the ONLY entry point to the support ticket system
- The route `/admin/support` (future) renders ticket inboxes, never workspace conversations

